  "solution": {
    "text": "In $P_{4}$ molecule, the four sp $^{3}$ -hybridised phosphorous atoms lie at the corners of a regular tetrahedron with $\\angle \\mathrm{PPP}=60^{\\circ}$.\r\n\r\nIn $\\mathrm{S}_{8}$ molecule S-S-S angle is $107^{\\circ}$ rings.\r\n\r\nIn $\\mathrm{S}_{8}$ molecule $\\mathrm{S}-\\mathrm{S}-\\mathrm{S}$ angle is $107^{\\circ} \\mathrm{rings} .$\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/bCMNUWQbSz_47wNXjl6sKLPpZSFLyWgnN3wewtcz7tY.original.fullsize.png\">",
